# worktrees.env — single source of truth for the parallel-Claude worktree set.
# Sourced by spawn-worktrees.sh, tmux-multi-claude.sh, and cleanup.sh.
#
# SLUGS[i]    flat name used for: the directory under .claude/worktrees/ and
#             the tmux session. Must not contain '/'.
# BRANCHES[i] actual git branch backing that worktree. May contain '/'.
#
# Keep the two arrays the same length and in matching order.
#
# Coverage maps to ../grouped/plans/ — one worktree per grouped-plan slice in
# that directory (slices 00–09). Each slice file's "Files this group owns"
# section is the only path set that worktree is allowed to modify.
#   foundation:           Wave 1 blocking contract layer — Astro scaffold,
#                         dependencies, both palettes, fonts, dark-default
#                         theme script, shared types, content schemas, UI
#                         primitives, and stubs for every cross-group
#                         component.
#   layout-chrome:        The persistent shell — glass header with nav, the
#                         theme-toggle island, two footers, and the four
#                         layouts, replacing the group 00 stubs with
#                         byte-identical prop signatures.
#   animated-background:  Four-layer hero backdrop — drifting aurora blobs,
#                         masked grid, bouncing tech icons, noise overlay.
#                         Under ~5 KB gz and fully static under
#                         prefers-reduced-motion.
#   homepage:             Every homepage section and the assembled `/` route —
#                         nine sections, roughly thirteen components, the
#                         largest surface in the project.
#   journal-taxonomy:     Journal index, category archives, and series pages,
#                         plus the shared BlogCard and CoverArt components the
#                         other groups depend on.
#   article:              Long-form reading experience — article hero, sticky
#                         table of contents, prose stylesheet, code blocks,
#                         tables, author box, related reading, series nav.
#   seo-404-feeds:        Discoverability and sharing — the Seo component every
#                         layout depends on, structured data, the 404 route,
#                         RSS feed, sitemap config, and build-time OG images.
#   content-data:         Everything the other groups render — taxonomy data,
#                         sample posts, typed portfolio data modules, and
#                         static public assets, as an editable scaffold.
#   infra:                Wave 1 independent AWS stack in Terraform — S3,
#                         CloudFront, ACM, Route 53 — plus the GitHub Actions
#                         build, deploy, and plan workflows.
#   integration:          Wave 3, runs alone — resolve seams between groups,
#                         replace remaining stubs, full verification, close the
#                         CSP hash loop, reconcile astro.md with what shipped.

SLUGS=(
  foundation
  layout-chrome
  animated-background
  homepage
  journal-taxonomy
  article
  seo-404-feeds
  content-data
  infra
  integration
)

BRANCHES=(
  feature/foundation
  feature/layout-chrome
  feature/animated-background
  feature/homepage
  feature/journal-taxonomy
  feature/article
  feature/seo-404-feeds
  feature/content-data
  feature/infra
  feature/integration
)
